Test the output of bands and dos with key word "mem_saver"

The fixed-density NSCF calculation checks bands to 1e-8 eV. Its former
automatically selected diagonalization threshold, 1.25e-10, allowed the last
printed digit of one CG band to cross the comparison boundary on CPU and GPU.
Use pw_diag_thr=1e-12 to resolve the bands reliably, retaining the charge input,
reference files, and comparison tolerances. CG bands then agree with a tighter
Davidson-subspace control within 2e-11 eV; CG controls at 1e-14 agree across CPU
and GPU within 2e-13 eV.

Set pw_diag_nmax=100 so a PPCG substitution also reaches this stricter residual
target. At the former budget of 50 it passed the observable checks but retained
inner residual warnings. Budgets 100 and 200 give identical converged outputs
in CPU and GPU controls, with no inner warning at 100. The larger ceiling does
not extend CG solves that already meet their stopping criterion.

